WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.767
FP32 supplies the share warm start.

2
00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:10.032
FP64 handles correction, final residual
checks, prices, output, exits and moments.

3
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.650
The predictor runs at most sixteen rounds,
with a looser tolerance.

4
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.605
It only prepares a guess;

5
00:00:18.605 --> 00:00:22.123
the FP64 checks decide whether the answer
is accepted.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.155
Convert the predicted shares to FP64,

7
00:00:27.155 --> 00:00:30.896
normalize them, then apply the original
correction rule.

8
00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:35.572
If the prediction is unusable, restore the
original FP64 initialization.

9
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.805
Recompute the residual of the returned
shares.

10
00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.261
Check it, the residual when the solver

11
00:00:41.261 --> 00:00:45.119
stopped, the number of updates, and that
every value is finite.

12
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.080
The predictor may change the iteration
path.

13
00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.421
Keep the final accuracy, check every

14
00:00:53.421 --> 00:00:57.322
economic result, and measure speed only
after those checks pass.
